msgid ""
"In order for a connection to be made, all of the policies that affect "
"compatibility must be compatible. For example, even if a requested and "
"offered QoS profile pair has compatible reliability QoS policies, but they "
"have incompatible durability QoS policies, a connection will still not be "
"made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:291
msgid ""
"When connections are not made, no messages will be passed between the "
"publisher and subscription. There are mechanisms to detect this situation, "
"which will be covered in a later section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:297
msgid ""
"Historically in ROS 1, any publisher and subscriber with the same message "
"type on the same topic would be connected. The possibility of incompatible "
"requested and offered QoS profiles is something new to be aware of when "
"using ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:303
msgid "QoS events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:305
msgid ""
"Some QoS policies have possible events related to them. Developers may "
"provide each publisher and subscription with callback functions that are "
"triggered by these QoS events and handle them in a way they see fit, similar "
"to how messages received on a topic are handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:308
msgid ""
"Developers may subscribe to the following QoS events that are associated "
"with a publisher:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:310
msgid "Offered deadline missed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:312
msgid ""
"The publisher has not published a message within the expected duration that "
"was set out by the deadline QoS policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:314
msgid "Liveliness lost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:316
msgid ""
"The publisher has failed to indicate its liveliness within the lease "
"duration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:318
msgid "Offered incompatible QoS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:320
msgid ""
"The publisher has encountered a subscription on the same topic that is "
"requesting a QoS profile that the offered QoS profile cannot satisfy, "
"resulting in no connection between the publisher and that subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:322
msgid ""
"Developers may subscribe to the following QoS events that are associated "
"with a subscription:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:324
msgid "Requested deadline missed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:326
msgid ""
"The subscription has not received a message within the expected duration "
"that was set out by the deadline QoS policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:328
msgid "Liveliness changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:330
msgid ""
"The subscription has noticed that one or more publishers on the subscribed "
"topic has failed to indicate their liveliness within the lease duration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:332
msgid "Requested incompatible QoS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:334
msgid ""
"The subscription has encountered a publisher on the same topic that is "
"offering a QoS profile that does not satisfy the requested QoS profile, "
"resulting in no connection between the subscription and that publisher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:339
msgid "Matched events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:341
msgid ""
"In addition to QoS events, matched events can be generated when any "
"publisher and subscription establishes or drops the connection between them. "
"Developers may provide each publisher and subscription with callback "
"functions that are triggered by matched events and handle them in a way they "
"see fit, similar to how messages received on a topic are handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:344
msgid ""
"Developers can subscribe to this event with a publisher or a subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:346
msgid ""
"publisher: this event happens when it finds a subscription which matches the "
"topic and has compatible QoS or a connected subscription is disconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:347
msgid ""
"subscription: this event happens when it finds a publisher which matches the "
"topic and has compatible QoS or a connected publisher is disconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:349
msgid "There are demos showing how to use the event:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:351
msgid ""
"rclcpp: `demo code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/"
"demo_nodes_cpp/src/events/matched_event_detect.cpp>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:352
msgid ""
"rclpy: `demo code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/demo_nodes_py/"
"demo_nodes_py/events/matched_event_detect.py>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:357
msgid "QoS overrides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:359
msgid ""
"By default, QoS profiles are specified directly in source code when "
"constructing publishers and subscriptions. However, ROS 2 also provides a "
"mechanism to override QoS profiles at node startup using ROS 2 parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:362
msgid ""
"When a node opts in to QoS overrides, it declares read-only parameters under "
"the ``qos_overrides`` namespace using the structure ``qos_overrides."
"<topic_name>.<entity_type>[_<id>].<policy_name>``. Users can then "
"reconfigure policies such as reliability, history depth, or durability using "
"YAML parameter files or command-line arguments without recompiling or "
"modifying the node source code. Additionally, applications can provide "
"validation callbacks to enforce safety constraints on user-supplied "
"overrides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Quality-of-Service-Settings.rst:366
msgid ""
"To learn how to enable and configure QoS overrides with hands-on examples, "
"see the :doc:`Configuring QoS overrides using parameters tutorial <Working-"
"with-topics/Configuring-QoS-Overrides>`."
msgstr ""

